 "sourceUrl": "https://e-file.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/1df5f09736174bdcaed9ea4e9276bf8b/M3T1A669N1188254859888107676/OptiXtrans%20E9612%20-.pdf",
 "notes": "Slot map from the E9612 Subrack chapter (333,351 B, 6 pp), E3CTU table: \"DC power supply: IU1-IU13\", \"AC or HVDC power supply: IU3-IU13\", with one APIU occupying physical IU1 and IU2 (logical IU1) under AC/HVDC - so 13 service board slots on DC, 11 on AC/HVDC, for a master or a slave subrack. The older AUX+SCC layout prints 12 (DC), 10 (AC master) and 11 (AC slave). This spec is the E3CTU DC build; an optional TMF1EFI takes IU13 (logical IU72) and would cost one service slot. Brochure agrees: \"Max. number of service board slots: 13\". Ports: TNG1N210 is \"10 x 10 Gbit/s Line Service Processing Board\" in the boards-overview Table 3, valid in the E9612 subrack; 13 slots x 10 = 130, each a 10G optical line (OTU2/OTU2e) interface in an SFP+ cage. The cage is derived from the 10G optical line rate - the board datasheet with the front panel (EDOC1100163901) is behind the support wall (302 -> /view/notFound). Build provenance. The frame half is vendor-stated: `https://e-file.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/0f9e00e3f2ca431693884a01667d7ec6/M3T1A669N1188254857740624027/OptiXtrans%20E9600%20Family%20-.pdf` (Product Brochure, 277,705 B) prints the \"Max. number of service board slots\" row, and the subrack chapters print the slot map. The card half is vendor-stated too, but from a partner mirror rather than a Huawei host: `https://www.actfornet.com/solutions/solution/OptiXtrans_E9600_Boards_Overview` (HTTP 200, 226,637 B) reproduces the hedex chapter *OptiXtrans E9600 (E9624/E9612/E9605) Boards Overview* (`EDOC1100126589`) and carries Table 3, \"Mapping between the line boards and OptiXtrans 9800 E9624/E9612/E9605 subrack\", whose TNG1N206/TNG1N210 row reads E9624 \"1:1 mode: Y 1:3 mode: Y\", E9612 \"Y\", E9605 \"Y\". That is the board-to-subrack validity no Huawei-hosted document publishes (the board chapters answer 302 -> /view/notFound; see research/optixtrans-client-board-chapters.md). The complement is a build recorded here, not a vendor configuration: every service slot is filled with the same line board, the convention devices/huawei/optixtrans-e6616.json and devices/arista/7504r.json already use. A shelf with tributary (TNG1T212/TNG1A212) or WSS boards fitted in some slots is a different box with a different port list.",
 "aliases": [
  "E9612"
 ]
}
